    psi: preserve indexed observations through normal call completion (#1074)
    
    * psi: preserve indexed observations through normal call completion
    
    Retain observed disjoint cells at an exact captured store after RHS effects.
    Share selected public-contract bindings and normal guarantees between value
    and statement calls, with real statement handles owning fresh output identity.
    Use current specification selectors and checked collection-predicate element
    consequences through the existing typed observation readers.
    
    All nine frozen indexed-handback places refuse at base
     a91a8de86514f5b0ba71509b3af4d656916d6062. The optimized Linux x86_64 repair
    runs all nine plus two additional positives with native/Terminal exits 0/0;
    15 invalid controls match their authored contract refusal. Pins are exact
    sample copies and each row twin changes only the store destination.
    
    Focused corpus: 31/33 positives execute 0/0; the two other refusals reproduce
    identically with the exact-base producer. All 43 selected invalids reject,
    41 at their authored reason; two old Build-API controls fail identically on
    base. Keep those limitations separate from the completed new row.
    
    * psi: record indexed handback execution and replay evidence
    
    * psi: retain indexed handback integration acceptance

